---
layout: base.njk
title: "Pricing: $0 per creator, at any earnings"
description: "Inflowwww costs $0 per creator profile per month, at any earnings. One card per platform, and Infloww's earnings-based price ladder as captured from infloww.com/pricing."
---
{#- Follows infloww.com/pricing (captured 2026-10-11): plans, earnings slider, questions, trial. The FAQ is wired in separately.
    The real cost sits above the four $0 cards on purpose: it is what a visitor searching for pricing came for. -#}
<section id="plans" aria-labelledby="plans-title" class="wrap pt-16 max-lg:pb-16 sm:pt-24">
  <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
  <h1 id="plans-title" class="h-page mt-2">Manage all your creators with one CRM, for $0 per creator</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every Inflowwww plan is the same repository (the project's source folder): every feature it has, under the MIT license, on your own server.
    The cards differ only in how much of each platform is built.
  </p>
  <p class="their-quote">Theirs: <q>Every Infloww plan includes all our unique features</q> (infloww.com/pricing, captured <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ site.captureDate }}</span>).</p>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl font-medium text-ink">
    Setup and updates mean typing a few commands on a server. After that, everyone on the team works in a browser.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl rounded-2xl bg-cream p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">What you do pay for</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink">
      The server you run it on, one proxy per creator if you want each on its own IP (you buy them; none are built in),
      any LLM usage, billed to you by the provider (the dashboard works without LLM keys), and your time: an evening to
      set up and lock down (see the <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/help/#security' | url }}">security notes</a>), then
      updates and backups.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3"><a class="text-link inline-flex min-h-11 items-center" href="{{ '/openinflowwww-vs-infloww/#stay' | url }}">Who should stay on Infloww</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{#- Below lg the earnings slider comes before the plan cards, so a phone sees the price question first; from lg up
    the cards sit right under the intro. Inside the slider block the order stays: controls, then the no-JS table. -#}
<div class="flex flex-col">
  <div class="wrap pt-10 pb-20 max-lg:pt-16 sm:pb-28">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
      {%- set planTos = true %}{% set planCompact = true %}
      {%- for id in ["onlyfans", "fansly", "mym", "fanvue"] %}
      {% set planId = id %}{% set planHeading = "h2" %}{% include "plan-card.njk" %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <section id="earnings" aria-labelledby="earnings-title" class="band-cream max-lg:order-first">
    <div class="wrap py-20 sm:py-28">
      <p class="eyebrow">The earnings slider</p>
      <h2 id="earnings-title" class="section-title mt-2">What each earnings bracket costs, per creator</h2>
      <p class="lede">Their OnlyFans and Fansly cards price each creator profile by the creator's monthly earnings. Pick a bracket and a team size.</p>
      {#- grid-cols-1 below lg: an implicit auto track grows to the ladder table's min-content width and pushes the page sideways at 320px. -#}
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,2fr)_minmax(0,3fr)]" data-earnings-slider>
        {%- set sliderTableWhere = "beside this panel, or below it on phones" %}
        {%- set sliderNote = "Under $500: $0. Over $75,000: still $0." %}
        {% include "pricing-block.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title" class="wrap py-20 sm:py-28">
  <h2 id="questions-title" class="section-title">Questions? The README is here to help.</h2>
  <p class="lede">If the README doesn't answer it, open an issue on GitHub.</p>
  <p class="their-quote">Theirs: a <q>Questions? We’re here to help.</q> block with a Book a demo button (infloww.com/pricing, captured <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ site.captureDate }}</span>).</p>
  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a class="btn-primary" href="{{ site.repo }}#readme">Read the README</a>
    <a class="btn-secondary" href="{{ site.repo }}/issues">Open an issue</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="trial" aria-labelledby="trial-title" class="band-cream">
  <div class="wrap py-20 sm:py-28">
    <h2 id="trial-title" class="section-title">What the trial looks like</h2>
    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card bg-white ring-1 ring-black/10">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Theirs</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
          A Start free trial button on every card, and <q>No credit card required</q> (infloww.com, captured <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ site.captureDate }}</span>).
          Their pricing page doesn't state a trial length. Their Fansly launch post says <q>Sign up for a 7-day free trial</q>
          (infloww.com/blog/introducing-infloww-for-fansly, their page stamped Oct 10, 2026).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card bg-white ring-1 ring-black/10">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Ours</h3>
        <pre class="mt-3 rounded-2xl bg-ink p-4 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-sm whitespace-pre text-mint"><code>git clone {{ site.repo }}.git openinflowwww
cd openinflowwww</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          No credit card required, because there is no card form. The command downloads the project's source folder; then follow the Quick start in the README.
          Nothing expires: the code is MIT licensed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "faq.njk" %}

